<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- OstrichChallenge: FRILIOTH

     The survivor on the radio, and the trader at the end of the drive. He is Fril, deliberately:
     the broadcast introduces him by name on day one, so the player knows who they are hearing long
     before they ever see him.

     WHERE THE FACE VALUES CAME FROM. Not from a screenshot, and not from me guessing. The character
     creator shows the parts as NUMBERS ("Face 04", "Eyes 24") while archetypes.xml wants NAMES
     ("Green04"), and nothing in the config maps one to the other: that list lives in the game's own
     resources. So the mod grew an "occ archetype" command that reads the player's live archetype
     out of EModelSDCS and prints it in this format, and this line is its output with the name
     changed from BaseMale to Frilioth.

         Face 04  -> variant="4"
         Eyes 24  -> eye_color="Green04"
         Hair Style 00, Mustache 00, Chops 00, Beard 00 -> omitted entirely

     THE OMISSIONS ARE DELIBERATE. Vanilla's bald archetypes (James, Denzel, Chong) simply have no
     hair attribute rather than an empty one, and only the archetypes with facial hair declare it.

     ==================================================================================
     THE CLOTHES (v0.76.1), AND WHY THEY ARE NOT THE ROGUE OUTFIT FRIL ASKED FOR
     ==================================================================================
     Fril wanted armorRogueOutfit and armorPreacherBoots. Three attempts went at that the direct
     way and all three failed, each one measured rather than assumed:

       armour slots     Equipment.SetSlotItem put both items on him, confirmed in the log, and
                        nothing rendered.
       cosmetic slots   UnlockCosmeticItem + SetCosmeticSlot both succeeded, "2 cosmetic(s) set",
                        and nothing rendered.
       the rebuild      not the cause. The log showed emodel EModelSDCS, a live animator with
                        enabled=True, and three forced UpdateEquipment calls.

     So worn armour and cosmetics do not render on a non-player SDCS NPC. What DOES work is this
     file's own <equipment>, because it is the same machinery that already gives him Fril's face.

     AND THE ROGUE OUTFIT HAS NO GEAR PREFAB. The "occ gear" command asks the game to load all 43
     candidate names taken from items.xml, and exactly 17 resolve, which is the sixteen sets vanilla
     archetypes use (Lumberjack answering to both spellings). Rogue is not among them: it exists as
     armour and cosmetic art only. The full found list is

         Assassin, Biker, Commando, Enforcer, Farmer, Fiber, Fitness, Lumberjack, Miner, Nerd,
         Nomad, Preacher, Raider, Ranger, Scavenger, Stealth

     Fril chose LumberJack for the body and Preacher for the boots. Both strings below are copied
     from prefabs the game confirmed it can load, not typed from memory.

     NO HANDS LINE, DELIBERATELY. Fril asked for a body and boots. I added LumberJack hands on the
     grounds that vanilla fills all three slots, he told me to take them off, and he was right: it
     was scope he had not asked for. His hands are bare, which vanilla does too (Jesse and Jade
     carry the Fiber set with empty excludes on hands and feet for exactly that).

     {sex} is vanilla's own token and resolves per archetype; every vanilla entry uses it.
     excludes hides the body part underneath so it cannot poke through, and vanilla sets it to the
     slot's own name 30 times out of 32.
-->
<configs>

    <append xpath="/archetypes">
        <archetype name="Frilioth" male="true" race="White" variant="4" eye_color="Green04">
            <equipment transform_name="body"  prefab="@:Entities/Player/{sex}/Gear/LumberJack/gear{sex}LumberJackPrefab.prefab" excludes="body"/>
            <equipment transform_name="feet"  prefab="@:Entities/Player/{sex}/Gear/Preacher/gear{sex}PreacherPrefab.prefab" excludes="feet"/>
        </archetype>
    </append>

</configs>
